members of ukraine security services run  for cover as the sound of a shell cuts  through the air and explodes close by  in the basement a group of elderly  residents is hiding  during a brief lull they emerge from the  shelter dazed and terrified  the police tell them to get into the  vehicle quickly  another shell explodes  their car passes a body on the street  just a few kilometers south the wreckage  of what were people's homes still burns  this is lizzy chansk one of the two  remaining cities that russia doesn't  control in the luganz region  the ukrainian army says russian forces  have destroyed the last of three bridges  that used to connect the city with  neighboring sierra donetsk over the  river to the north  potentially making it very difficult for  soldiers volunteer units and what the  ukrainian military says are many  civilians refusing to leave or trapped  inside  we are civilians why are they shelling  us as if junior we don't have anyone  here no soldiers why are they bombing  says her friend  they stand by a grave where one of their  two neighbours was hastily buried in  recent days  and they all ask this question why don't  you leave but where are we supposed to  go this is our land we grow up here we  live here our mothers and fathers are  buried here in the cemetery  these residents line up to get water  from a fire truck ukrainian authorities  say there's been no water or electricity  for days  unexploded rockets are stuck in the  earth and rubble people here say russian  shelling is increasing all the time  they started shooting very hard  many people began to leave  or at least the ones who had somewhere  to go  military analysts say most of ukraine's  soviet-built weaponry has been destroyed  ukrainian army says it needs more  long-range artillery and tanks if it is  to stop the russian advance ukraine's  western partners have already sent or  promised to send military hardware worth  billions of dollars ukraine says it's  nowhere near sufficient and it's not  getting to the front lines fast enough  as nato defense ministers are scheduled  to meet in brussels on wednesday there  are many ukrainians increasingly asking  whether the west can sustain or even  build upon its level of military support  charles stratford al jazeera kiev
 

